        {
          "path": "_m/r/5/v/m/lark-quarry-dinosaur-trackways-wp/weekend-magazine-visits-larks-.jpg",
          "filename": "Weekend Magazine visits Larks Quarry.jpg",
          "caption": "The Larks Quarry dinosaur stampede tracks were first uncovered by a pastoral station manager in the 1960s. Palaeontologists from UQ and Qld Museum made further investigations in the late 1970s. In 1982 the Queensland National Parks and Wildlife Service invited a team from the ABC's Weekend Magazine to film at the site. In the years since there have been Interpretation Centres built around the site. Unfortunately after two separate collapses of these buildings, much of the original footprints have had to be replaced with replicas obtained from plaster casts. This picture shows the ABC team at the site in 1982.",
